Open the Games Aquarium room
  Load the existing simulation and create a raised tank with one cell per simulation position.
  Draw walls and distinct shapes and colors for builders, breakers, and hunters.
  Advance the world every 230 milliseconds while the room is active and running.
  Pause or resume, step once when paused, or restore the original world.
  Choose a species and select a tank cell to place it through the simulation's placement rules.
  Report placement, tick, creature, wall, and catch status on the board.
  Keep visitors outside the raised tank and allow walking or teleporting around it.
  On re-entry, keep the world and restart the tick clock.
